WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.080
- Earlier this season,
comedian Deon Cole was here

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.770
telling us about his movie
"The Harder They Fall,"

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.750
and while he wasn't at
the "SNL 40th Anniversary"

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.660
after-party, I'm assuming
my invitation as well

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.440
was misplaced at the printer,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.930
cool, it's fine, I
didn't want to go anyway,

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.780
Deon and I, we had better things to do,

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.690
but he did have lots to say
about some other "SNL" legends.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.250
So watch this.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.530
So you're back to traveling
a bit for your stand-ups.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.363
So is that exciting?

00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:27.200
Are you a good traveler?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.920
- Yeah, I mean, yeah, I mean, definitely.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.340
We out hitting the road
again, doing our shows

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.000
and stuff and you know.
- That's cool.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.130
- I'm a decent traveler.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.420
I travel as light as possible though.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.530
That's, see, that's what's
wrong with a lot of people,

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.025
when you travel, you take
too many what if clothes,

00:00:42.025 --> 00:00:42.882
(audience laughing)

00:00:42.882 --> 00:00:44.800
and you know you're not gonna
wear them what if clothes.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:45.950
You know you not.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.790
- This is true.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.700
- You know, or you bring your fat clothes

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.831
and your skinny clothes.

00:00:49.831 --> 00:00:50.664
(Kelly laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:00:50.664 --> 00:00:51.846
- I just bring the fat ones.

00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:52.759
- You just bring the?

00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:53.592
(Deon laughing)
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:54.530
- I just don't even dream big.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.779
I'm just like, I'm bringing the cozies.

00:00:56.779 --> 00:00:58.110
- Yeah, I bring all my big clothes and if

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.560
I do get skinny, then I go shopping.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.596
- That's what you
deserve for being skinny.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.564
That's motivating.
- That's what you deserve.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.521
(audience applauding)

00:01:05.521 --> 00:01:09.230
if you get skinny, your reward is to shop.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.229
- I like this.

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:12.040
- And that's what I say,
yeah, so that's what I do.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.300
I make sure I roll up all
my clothes so everything

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.930
get in there, but there's
no in between clothes.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.836
Either I look bummy or I'm super clean.

00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:20.806
That's it.
- Me too.

00:01:20.806 --> 00:01:21.639
(audience laughing)
Me too.

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:23.660
Who are these people
that, at like airports,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.960
and they're literally like, I mean,

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.500
heeled out, like, full
on suit or like full,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.700
it's all done, I'm like, where are you,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.200
are you going directly
there when you land?

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.650
Like, like where are your comfy clothes?

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.390
- I think they get the, I
think the information is

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.360
if you in business class
or something like that,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.030
you have to be dressed up or whatever.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:43.960
That's how it used to be.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.136
- They must look at me
like, how did you get here?

00:01:46.136 --> 00:01:47.510
(audience laughing)

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:50.730
I'm usually in like comfy travel wear.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.474
Anyway, I'm not trying to impress anyone.

00:01:52.474 --> 00:01:53.990
So, and I'm like, do
you think you're going

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:54.940
to meet them on the plane?

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.199
All right, cool.

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:59.040
Do you ever ask other comedians,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.530
like for their input, like on your jokes?

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.080
- Yeah, I mean some, well
I don't ask for my input,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.350
but if we think of
something at the same time,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.220
we'll sit there and
goes, yo, you want that?

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.970
I can have that, or you can have that,

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.510
and then we go like that or whatever.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.713
- [Kelly] It's like songwriters.

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:14.580
- But every blue moon I like, I was,

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.820
I would go like to a
comedian and ask them,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:18.920
is this cool or not?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.430
You know, like, I'll call up
Dave Chappelle and be like,

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.200
hey, let me know how you
feel about this joke.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.956
He never calls back, but.

00:02:25.956 --> 00:02:27.040
(audience laughing)

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.180
- Maybe that's how he felt.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.013
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.013 --> 00:02:31.570
I call, I call up Chris Rock, hey.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:32.610
Never calls back.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.790
Sin, never calls back.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.910
So I end up doing it my own self.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:37.743
- [Kelly] I know, I love it.

00:02:37.743 --> 00:02:40.580
- Yeah, either it work or it don't work.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.790
- That's how you find out.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.470
It lands or it doesn't.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.480
So wait, so wait, have
you had a chance to meet?

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.680
I know you, they won't answer your calls,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.500
apparently any of those comedians,

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.750
but like have you had a chance to meet?

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.509
- Hey Sinbad, call me back, all right?

00:02:52.509 --> 00:02:53.342
If you can, Sinbad.

00:02:53.342 --> 00:02:55.410
- But any of your idols,
have you been able to like,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.630
I don't know, hang with them at all, or.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:57.970
- Man, yeah.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.020
Man, a lot of 'em.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.080
I just, man, Eddie Murphy.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.913
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:03:01.913 --> 00:03:03.000
- Man, yeah.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.019
Give it up for Eddie.

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:04.941
(audience applauding)

00:03:04.941 --> 00:03:06.170
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.266
- [Deon] Yeah, I was with Eddie.

00:03:07.266 --> 00:03:08.690
- [Kelly] He's one of my faves.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.500
- I remember when
"Dreamgirls" was happening,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.850
I was leaving this event and the,

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.800
no, I was coming to the
event and he was leaving

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.410
and I was like, oh my God, it's Eddie,

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.870
and I was standing behind
him and I just leaned over,

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:20.850
and I said, hey, how you doing?

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:22.270
I know you don't know
me, but I'm gonna work

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.567
with you one day, and he just
looked at me and was like.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.950
- He was like, stage five clinger.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.860
- Yeah, yeah, 'cause I
was leaning, had that

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.942
Michael Jackson lean too, I was like,

00:03:32.942 --> 00:03:34.708
(audience laughing)

00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:36.070
hey I know you don't know me but I'm going

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.296
to be working with him
one day, I know that.

00:03:38.296 --> 00:03:40.453
- And it's not meant to be creepy at all.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:44.049
- Yeah, yeah, but then here we
are later, I was at a party,

00:03:44.049 --> 00:03:46.297
a Netflix party, and he came up to me

00:03:46.297 --> 00:03:49.690
and told me he enjoyed my work and.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.257
- Did he remember that, the other time?

00:03:51.257 --> 00:03:52.877
- No, he did not, he just came up to me.

00:03:52.877 --> 00:03:55.040
He was like, man, I'm a fan of your work,

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.280
and I couldn't believe it,

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.083
and yeah.
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:03:58.083 --> 00:04:00.130
- And, and also now I'm
working with him too so.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.089
- That's so cool.

00:04:01.089 --> 00:04:02.377
(audience applauding)

00:04:02.377 --> 00:04:03.210
I love that.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.683
I love when you meet people
you love and they're cool.

00:04:05.683 --> 00:04:06.516
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:06.516 --> 00:04:07.640
He's super cool.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.340
He's like super cool, and he has

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.520
a lot of knowledge too, man.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.545
Like, he was telling me
about "Trading Places,"

00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:17.906
the amount of money he made
on that, on "Trading Places."

00:04:17.906 --> 00:04:19.170
- Yeah, I love that you were like.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.120
- I was like this.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.300
I would have made "Trading Places."

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.460
- [Kelly] Like for a third of that.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.610
- Oh, no, it was nothing.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.110
- Oh, I thought you were
saying you were brag,

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.333
'cause he was like, I made a ton of money.

00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:29.520
- No, that was something they would have

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.250
paid me to pay, to do "Trading Spaces."

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.083
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:35.380
- No, they gave him like
nothing really for that.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.400
- [Kelly] Oh wow.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.030
- Yeah, that's what he told me.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:38.943
He told me that one time, yeah.

00:04:38.943 --> 00:04:41.830
- That's why the next
time around you go, nope.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.970
- Yeah, but the next
time he made up for that.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.670
- [Kelly] Yeah, I would
have too if I were him.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:48.100
- I'm quite sure, yeah, yeah.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:48.980
That's how you gotta do.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.377
- I thought you were saying,
yeah, he told me how much money

00:04:50.377 --> 00:04:52.171
